  "tipSettings": {
    "tips": [
      "Ten costs nothing to maintain and shields you from Nen attacks. Drop it — fall into Zetsu or hit zero aura — and even an ordinary fist can gut you.",
      "Aura is a finite bar. Ren, Hatsu, En, and Ko all spend it. Burn it to zero and you collapse into defenseless, exhausted Zetsu until you rest.",
      "A vow buys power, but its condition is absolute. Break the condition and the ability simply does not fire — and the backlash can savage your aura.",
      "Your Nen category decides what comes easily. Working against your nature on the hexagon is possible, but it costs more aura and delivers less.",
      "Most people cannot see Nen and don't know it exists. To a civilian your aura is just an impossible feat — and impossible feats draw dangerous attention.",
      "Not every conflict is a fight. This world settles things with wagers, games, and tests as often as fists. Winning without a blow is a real victory.",
      "Money is Jenny, and the numbers run large: a meal costs thousands, a professional's work millions, an auction treasure hundreds of millions or more.",
      "A Hunter License is among the most valuable things you can own — it opens doors, forgives sins, and makes powerful people listen. Earning one is brutal.",
      "Death is never clean here. Survive a killing blow and you carry the cost: a scar, a crippling wound, a debt, or years of your life bargained away.",
      "Water Divination reveals your Nen type. A leaf, a glass of water, and your aura — how the water changes names which of the six categories is yours.",
      "Strength answers strength. An armed mob is lethal to the unawakened and background noise to a trained Nen user. Always read which you are facing.",
      "Each story start is sealed to one era of the tale. The narrator will not spoil what comes later — and the world reacts only to what this era knows."
    ],
    "tipDisplayEnabled": true,
    "tipTurnInterval": 10,
    "tipMinimumTurns": 4,
    "tipMaximumTurns": 40
  },
